1
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,500
大家好，欢迎来到 NASA 发射台
Hey there, welcome to NASA Launch Pad.

2
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,100
我是主持人安伯·韦伦
I'm your host, Amber Whalen.

3
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:24,900
好的，质量是物体所含物质的多少，这个概念很简单，对吧？
Okay, so you know that mass is the amount of matter in an object. Kind of a simple concept, right?

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:29,300
物体的质量不会随引力变化，那才是重量
An object's mass doesn't change due to the gravitational pull. That's weight.

5
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:37,300
但质量确实会影响其他多个特性，这些特性就叫质量特性
But the mass of an object does have relevance to several other properties. And those properties are called, wait for it, mass properties.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:44,000
那这些特性是什么，又有什么意义呢？要回答这个问题，阿曼达·卡特赖特是最合适的人选
Now, what are these properties and what do they mean? Well, to answer that question, who better to turn to than Amanda Cutright?

7
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:52,000
她是质量特性工作组负责人，支持猎户座飞行测试办公室的飞行测试文章项目
She is the Mass Properties Working Group lead supporting the Orion Flight Test Office through the Abort Flight Test Flight Test Articles Project.

8
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:54,400
这放不下字幕底部标题。
That won't fit in the lower third title.

9
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,600
所以我们叫她机械工程师，她确实也是。
So we're going to call her a mechanical engineer, which she is also.

10
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:04,500
说到质量特性，其实包含很多不同的特性。
When I mention mass properties, there are a lot of different properties contained in there.

11
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,600
最常见的就是质量，还有重心。
The ones most commonly known are the mass, and then there's also a center of gravity.

12
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:13,900
也就是说，质量可以等效集中到一个点上。
So that's kind of the point where that mass could basically be reflected in one point.

13
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:19,800
比如用刀刃平衡物体，重心要放在刀刃上才能保持平衡。
So if you were balancing it on a knife, that center of gravity is what you would need to put over that knife to make it balanced.

14
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:29,600
还有惯性，它取决于质量以及质量离重心或目标点的距离。
And there's also an inertia component, which is a function of the mass and how far away that mass is from the center of gravity or the point that you want the inertia to be.

15
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,800
那我们快速回顾一下。
So, let's recap real quick.

16
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:38,400
阿曼达提到的两大特性，除了质量，就是惯性和重心。
The two big properties that Amanda mentioned, besides mass, are inertia and the center of gravity.

17
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,200
回到牛顿第一定律
Go back to Newton's first law.

18
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:47,900
静止的物体保持静止，运动的物体保持匀速直线运动，除非受到外力
An object at rest stays at rest, and an object in motion stays in motion at the same speed and direction unless some new force comes on the scene.

19
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:53,500
现实点说，你得有个外力才会从沙发上站起来
Let's face it, the only way you're going to get off that couch is when some outside force drives you to do so.

20
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:57,000
比如饿了、妈妈喊你，或者内急
Like hunger, your mother yelling at you, or nature calling.

21
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:01,300
因为所有物体都不愿意无缘无故改变状态
That's because all objects really hate to change what they're doing without a good reason.

22
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:07,100
科学家把这叫惯性，即物体对运动状态改变的阻力位
And that's something scientists call inertia, or the resistance of an object to make change in the state of motion.

23
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,200
物体惯性质量越大，对运动状态改变的阻力位就越大
But the higher the inertial mass of an object, the larger the resistance to changing its state of motion.

24
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:22,100
所以两个质量不同的物体，质量大的加速度小，质量小的加速度大
So, if you had two objects with different masses, the object with the larger mass will experience a smaller acceleration, and the object with the smaller mass will experience a bigger acceleration.

25
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,800
重心也是重要的质量特性。
The center of gravity is another important property.

26
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:32,900
重力对物体各部分拉力相同，所以重心就是系统重量平衡的点。
Remember that gravity is pulling equally on all parts of an object. So an object's center of gravity is the point in which the system's weight is balanced.

27
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:38,300
但要注意，重心不一定和物体的几何中心重合。
But keep in mind, the center of gravity doesn't always correspond with the geometric center of an object.

28
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:49,700
比如跑车的重心设计得很低，急转弯更稳；大卡车重心高，急转弯容易翻车。
For example, the center of gravity in sports cars would be designed low to the ground to make for better handling on sharp turns, while the center of gravity in a big truck is much higher, making sudden turns a problem.

29
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:53,000
你觉得这些物体的重心在哪？
Where do you think the center of gravity is in some of these things?

30
00:03:01,236 --> 00:03:03,836
那这些质量特性如何影响飞行？
But how do those properties affect how something flies?

31
00:03:04,336 --> 00:03:05,736
还是请阿曼达来解释。
Here's Amanda again to explain.

32
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:11,336
这些特性会从多个角度影响飞行。
Those specific properties affect flight from a lot of different perspectives.

33
00:03:11,636 --> 00:03:15,036
主要体现在空气动力学和飞行动力学上
Probably the main ones are the aerodynamics and the flight dynamics.

34
00:03:15,036 --> 00:03:22,936
比如飞行轨迹，这也会影响飞行控制系统
So the path or trajectory the object is going to take, which also then goes into the avionics or the flight control systems that go into the article.

35
00:03:23,536 --> 00:03:27,836
还有结构和载荷方面的影响
And it also gets involved from a structure and load standpoint.

36
00:03:27,936 --> 00:03:34,136
质量和重心会影响系统各部件的受力
So the mass and that center of gravity affects how much load is going to be applied to certain components of the system.

37
00:03:35,636 --> 00:03:38,636
那飞行测试文章的这些特性也一样吗？
But are those properties going to be the same in a flight test article?

38
00:03:39,036 --> 00:03:48,536
比如战神1-X飞行测试文章，有些部件没有最终版的内部系统和结构
For example, in the Ares 1X flight test article, certain components aren't going to have all the same internal systems and structures that will go into the final Ares 1 vehicle.

39
00:03:49,136 --> 00:03:52,336
当然，战神1-X上也不会有宇航员
And of course, there won't be any astronauts going up in the Ares 1X.

40
00:03:53,036 --> 00:03:54,936
这对工程师来说是个挑战
This seems to be a challenge for engineers.

41
00:03:55,336 --> 00:03:57,836
阿曼达，你们怎么解决这个问题？
So, how do you handle that, Amanda?

42
00:03:59,236 --> 00:04:09,836
作为质量特性工程师，我们经常会被问到：飞行测试文章是否准确模拟了宇航员座位、卧铺和其他部件的位置？
So as a mass properties engineer, a question that comes up a lot is, are we actually accurately representing in our flight test articles where the astronauts are sitting and where their beds are and all the different components?

43
00:04:10,136 --> 00:04:22,736
答案是：实际飞行器会装载所有系统和宇航员，因此会有相应的质量和重心。
So the answer to that question is that the operational vehicle will have all of those systems in there, the astronauts in there, and therefore has a resulting mass and center of gravity point.

44
00:04:23,036 --> 00:04:31,036
而飞行测试文章要达到相同的质量和重心，但内部结构和子系统不同。
For our flight test articles, we have have to end up with the same mass and center of gravity point, but we have a different structure and different subsystems in there.

45
00:04:31,236 --> 00:04:43,936
比如在 Pad Abort 1 和接下来的 Centaur Abort 1 飞行测试中，我们会用数千磅压舱物来满足质量和 CG 要求。
So in our particular case for the PataBort 1 flight test, as well as the next flight test, which will be a CentaBort 1, we have thousands of pounds of ballast that we use to get to that mass and CG requirement.

46
00:04:45,436 --> 00:04:55,436
如果加入压舱物或其他重物来稳定飞行器，那飞行测试文章和最终产品有何区别呢？
So if they're putting ballast in, or some random heavy material added to help stabilize the object, that's got me wondering how these flight test articles compare to their final counterparts.

47
00:04:56,036 --> 00:04:57,136
这得看具体情况。
Well, it depends.

48
00:04:57,536 --> 00:05:00,036
不同飞行测试的目标和任务各不相同。
Different flight tests have different goals and objectives.

49
00:05:00,336 --> 00:05:06,936
所以飞行测试文章的部件不必完全一致，材料有时也不同
So not all parts of the flight test article need to be identical. And in some cases, the materials used may not even be the same.

50
00:05:07,236 --> 00:05:08,336
让阿曼达来解释
Let's let Amanda explain.

51
00:05:09,636 --> 00:05:17,936
我身后是‘上升者1号’飞行测试的隔热罩，我用它来举例，说明我们对所有测试部件的处理方式
So what you see behind me is the heat shield for the Ascensivore 1 flight test, and I'll use that as an example for something that we do on all the components that go into those flight tests.

52
00:05:18,236 --> 00:05:33,136
我们有个CAD模型，代表理想隔热罩的密度和形状，但会实际称重，再与分析模型对比
We have a CAD model that represents, computer-aided design model, that represents the ideal heat shield, so the density of and the shape of that particular part, but we actually take a measurement of what that actually weighs, and we compare it to the analytical model.

53
00:05:33,336 --> 00:05:41,636
在质量特性方面，我们既有来自多方的估算，也有每个部件的实际数据
So for mass properties, we have both estimates that come from a variety of areas, as well as the actuals for each component.

54
00:05:42,736 --> 00:05:44,536
阿曼达，感谢你的详细介绍
Thanks, Amanda, for all the information.

55
00:05:44,936 --> 00:05:47,936
反复测试，寻找最佳答案
Testing and retesting. Looking for the best answers.

56
00:05:48,436 --> 00:05:51,236
你以为草稿只存在大一英语作业里？
And you thought draft versions ended with freshman English.

57
00:05:51,936 --> 00:05:53,536
好，本期节目就到这里。
Well, that's it for this episode.

58
00:05:53,736 --> 00:05:56,736
我是安伯·韦伦，下期《NASA 发射台》再见。
I'm Amber Whalen. And we'll catch you next time on NASA Launch Pad.
